 # Unify idle and batched inbound message custom type
 
-Refactor Tattler/Chorus inbound delivery so the idle emit path and busy pending-batch path use the same custom message type, details shape, and renderer. The canonical content is the concatenated model-visible message text/XML; details contains messages[] for both cases. The idle case is just a one-element messages array. This should remove the split between old single-message custom types and tattler:pending-batch, reduce renderer branching, and keep visible/hidden filtering consistent.
-
+Doug decision from smoke: idle single-message delivery and busy batch delivery should use the same custom message type/struct/renderer. The one-message idle case is just a batch with count=1. Use one canonical Tattler message-batch custom type (currently tattler:pending-batch or renamed) with model-facing concatenated content and details {kind:"batch", batchId, messages:[...]}. Renderer filters/branches by item visibility/type, not idle vs busy origin. This should replace divergence between Chorus idle chorus-room-message and Tattler pending-batch. Benefits: one hidden/visible filtering path, one replay/restore/dedupe shape, one renderer, easier participant metadata and TAT-60 styling.
